// Trebuchet throw model, JavaScript port (Phase 9).
//
// A line-by-line port of the Python model in 04_model/trebuchet/ (params.py, dynamics.py,
// throw.py, flight.py, version 0.6.0) on the equations generated by 04_model/derive.py
// (06_simulator/generated/treb_eom.js, never edited by hand). Same stages, events, friction
// fixed point, drag, release modes, loads and energy books; symbols follow
// 03_engineering/notation.md. Angles are absolute, from the downward vertical, positive in
// the throwing sense, in RADIANS internally.
//
// Differences from the Python model (all numerical, none physical):
//   - integrator: Dormand-Prince 5(4) with its 4th-order dense output, instead of SciPy's
//     DOP853 (8th order); events are located on the dense output with Brent's method, as SciPy does;
//   - the release-window scan uses n_grid points (default 2001, as in Python) and the drag
//     search 81 flights, as in Python; tolerances are set by mc.rtol / mc.atol as in Python.
// Checked against the Python model in 06_simulator/crosscheck.md.
//
